From f0d5746fd29eef5d430c1a2cfb77409150560351 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:10:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 020/115] net: qrtr: turn QRTR into a bus

The upcoming iio/qcom_smgr driver talks to the Snapdragon Sensor Core
over QRTR as a per-service client: it needs to bind against a
service/instance pair the way a normal bus driver binds against a
device ID, not open-code its own NEW_SERVER/DEL_SERVER bookkeeping on
top of the raw qrtr socket API.

Give QRTR a driver model bus. qrtr_endpoint gains add_device()/
del_device() hooks; qrtr_endpoint_post() calls them when a
QRTR_TYPE_NEW_SERVER or QRTR_TYPE_DEL_SERVER control packet arrives,
registering/unregistering a struct qrtr_device on struct bus_type
qrtr_bus so struct qrtr_driver implementations (matched by service and
instance) get probed and removed as services come and go. The SMD
endpoint driver implements both hooks; endpoints that don't set them
(qrtr/mhi.c, qrtr/tun.c) are left alone -- add_device()/del_device()
are only invoked when non-NULL, so a control packet arriving over
qrtr-tun can't NULL-deref.

This is the same rework taimen-v6.0 carries (originally by Yassine
Oudjana), ported onto 6.18's current net/qrtr/af_qrtr.c. 6.18 already
has an upstream bounds check gating QRTR_TYPE_NEW_SERVER and
QRTR_TYPE_RESUME_TX on sizeof(struct qrtr_ctrl_pkt) before the payload
is touched; that check is extended to QRTR_TYPE_DEL_SERVER, which this
rework is what now dereferences pkt->server for.

Add include/linux/soc/qcom/qrtr.h (struct qrtr_device, struct
qrtr_driver, qrtr_driver_register()) here rather than in the later
qcom_smgr driver commit that consumes it: net/qrtr/smd.c needs it too,
and a driver-facing API header belongs with the infrastructure that
implements it, not with its first consumer -- otherwise this commit
would not build standalone. Also add the mod_devicetable.h /
scripts/mod/file2alias.c / scripts/mod/devicetable-offsets.c plumbing
MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(qrtr, ...) needs to generate a "qrtr:" modalias.

bus_type.match()/.uevent() and EXPORT_SYMBOL_NS_GPL()/
MODULE_IMPORT_NS() have all moved on since v6.0 (const struct
device_driver *, const struct device *, and string literal
namespaces respectively); adapted to 6.18's current signatures instead
of carrying the old ones forward.

Signed-off-by: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Co-developed-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
